  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 804 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThe long term forecast period will be characterized by a welcomed\npattern change. An upper level trough digs down across the Midwest\ntowards the Southeast during the middle of the week. This will push \na cold front through the area Tuesday night through Wednesday and as \na result, low to medium chances (30-60%) for showers and storms are \nexpected. As the upper level trough axis shifts to our east, \nnorthwest flow begins to advect in a noticeably cooler and drier \nairmass bringing some much needed relief from the heat. We begin to \nreally feel the drier air late Wednesday night into Thursday as \ndewpoints fall into the lower 60s. Afternoon highs Thursday through \nSaturday are forecast to only rise into the low to mid 80s with \novernight lows in the upper 50s to lower 60s.",
